I found 10 issues on `2026-10-05-tool-config-templates`, ranked most severe first below. I left out round 1–3 findings that the fix commits already resolved, and anything owned by the pending units (U6–U8 docs, the reshape-migration plan).

I confirmed the top finding by running the shipped `.config/dprint.json` (dprint 0.60.1) over a sample `tsconfig.json`: it adds trailing commas, and Python's `json.load`, which `check-json` uses, then refuses the file. The tool-config render and pack test suites pass (85/85). Everything else comes from reading the code and was not reproduced.

